==English==

===Etymology===
From {{suf|en|country|side}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈkʌn.tɹiˌsaɪd/}}
* {{audio|en|En-uk-countryside.ogg|Audio (UK)}}
* {{hyphenation|en|coun|try|side}}

===Noun===
{{wp|Rural area}}
{{en-noun}}

# An area located outside of [[town|towns]] and [[city|cities]]; an area that is not [[urban]] or [[suburban]]; a [[rural]] area.
# Such part of a larger area.
#: {{ux|en|We live in the Swedish '''countryside'''.}}
# A [[rural]] [[landscape]].

====Usage notes====
* Typically used with the [[definite article]].

